The provided `CompositeException` class is primarily a utility for aggregating and formatting exception information. Its typical usage involves constructing exception objects, retrieving messages, and printing stack traces—operations that are not performance‑critical paths in most applications. Micro‑benchmarking with JMH is most valuable for hot loops, algorithmic code, or APIs where latency and throughput are a concern. Consequently, generating JMH benchmarks for this class would not yield actionable performance insights.